                "added": [
                    "#* Going in a straight line above the electrical outlet, drill two small holes in the ceiling directly above the outlet. The holes should be drilled approximately {{convert|3|to|6|in|cm|1}} from the wall on which the outlet is located, and should be approximately {{convert|8|in|cm|1}} apart.",
                    "#* Make sure that the extended rabbit ears are sticking through the holes at least {{convert|2|to|3|in|cm|1}}, preferably even further. This will allow the rabbit ear antennas to receive the bounced signals from your home's electrical wiring."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#* Going in a straight line above the electrical outlet, drill two small holes in the ceiling directly above the outlet. The holes should be drilled approximately 3 to 6 inches from the wall on which the outlet is located, and should be approximately 8 inches apart.",
                    "#* Make sure that the extended rabbit ears are sticking through the holes at least 2 to 3 inches, preferably even further. This will allow the rabbit ear antennas to receive the bounced signals from your home's electrical wiring."
                ]
            }
